    fix(vouchers): SPA-VOUCHER-YEAR-001 — a mistyped expiry year 500'd voucher lookup
    
    Highbury could not take payment on SPA-S3DJU3NJ: /api/vouchers/lookup
    returned 'server error' for it. A browser date field accepts years up to
    275760, so one extra digit stored expires_at as year 202666. PG keeps that
    happily; node-postgres hands back a JS Date, and toISOString() then returns
    the EXPANDED form '+202666-09-30'. isExpired's slice(0,10) took
    '+202666-09', parsed a missing day, built an Invalid Date and threw
    RangeError on the next toISOString() — a 500 on every lookup of that
    voucher, with a customer at the till.
    
    Three layers:
    - isExpired can no longer throw. It reads UTC parts off a Date instead of
      slicing an ISO string, rejects years outside 1900-9999, and treats
      anything unreadable as NOT expired — refusing a good voucher over a typo
      in its expiry is the worse failure.
    - cleanExpiry() gates both POST and PUT: a date that is not a plain
      YYYY-MM-DD in 1900-2200 is refused with a message naming the year, so the
      bad value never reaches the column again.
    - Both voucher date inputs carry min/max, so the till stops offering a
      six-digit year in the first place.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
